SM(529,{"n":"1 Corinthians 2","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/1 Corinthians 2.mp3","d":2941.3,"s":[[0.16,"Come and study Holy Scriptures with us as Father Stephen DeYoung teaches verse by verse on the podcast The Whole Counsel of God."],[8.08,"Father Stephen is a former Protestant pastor and Bible teacher in the Reformed Church, but now an Orthodox priest serving at Archangel Gabriel Orthodox Church in Lafayette, Louisiana."],[20.88,"So we'll go ahead and get started, and uh when we get started, uh in just a few moments, we'll be picking up at the beginning of St."],[28.48,"Paul's First Epistle to the Corinthians chapter two."],[33.76,"And though it will uh likely be some time for us here at the time of this recording before you can hear last week's Bible study online, uh, because we're we've got a good lead going on uh the Bible study as it's being posted."],[49.92,"Uh eventually, and by the time anyone else is hearing this, you'll be able to go back and listen to my uh introduction."],[56.24,"Some of that material will come up again as we go through."],[59.44,"as We'll be revisiting some of it, some of the background material and that kind of thing we get to different parts uh of this letter."],[67.56,"But last time I talked a lot about Corinth and its history, and and uh we then went through uh chapter one, and as we mentioned, back when we went through the beginning of Romans, in his greetings and his introduction, St."],[82.28,"Paul tends to sort of plant all the seeds of where he's going, sort of with the epistle as a whole."],[89.32,"Sort of serves in the early part as an introduction, and then he sort of unpacks those different themes as he goes through."],[95.48,"So we saw some of those, and we saw that at least one of the problems, and as we mentioned last time, as we go through, we're gonna discover that. uh the church in Corinth has a lot of problems"],[108.48,"Um, but one of those problems, as we just saw last time in chapter one, is that there were a whole bunch of sort of factions developing, sort of little cults of personality, unintended, but uh where there were people in the church who were sort of forming parties, that they were followers of Saint Paul or followers of St."],[130.64,"Peter or followers of St."],[132.64,"Apollos, and some of them were trying to sort of be one upris on everybody and say, Well, there you follow only Christ, and thereby sort of trying to pit these people against each other and create these these other dynamics."],[146.24,"And so St."],[147.04,"Paul was denouncing this pretty strongly, making it very clear that he never intended this to happen, he never wanted this to happen, it shouldn't happen."],[155.74,"As he said, you know, uh Paul didn't die for them."],[160.72,"Paul didn't forgive their sins, it's not the gospel of Paul, that was preached to them."],[167.21,"Um, and so everyone is one in Christ because it's only Christ who can who can do these things."],[175.77,"And so, if we really understand that, then we wouldn't be forming these factions in the first place."],[182.25,"We'd be trying to follow Christ."],[184.49,"And this is not going to be the end, this is just the beginning of the problems."],[188.81,"Uh, we heard in his introduction when he was talking about some of the people who are with him, we kind of heard who the rat was."],[194.85,"That uh someone from that community had come to him where he was and uh sort of let him know some of the things that were going on in Corinth, and that that's a big part of what uh occasioned uh this letter."],[208.05,"We've seen that the approach St."],[210.13,"Paul is taking is not just to chide them or upbraid them, uh though there's been a little bit of that, and there's gonna be more of that, but that he's taken the approach of trying to remind them who it is they are in Christ and who it is God has called them to be."],[227.41,"Uh, and to take that approach of asking them to live up to that now."],[232.45,"This is who you are, this is who you're called to be, this is the destiny that's ahead of you in Christ."],[237.97,"We need to live up to that."],[240.97,"With strong, obvious implication that right now we're not."],[245.69,"We're not. So unless there are any questions or comments or anything left over, or just in general, we'll go ahead and get started at the beginning of chapter two."],[262.49,"So he says, and I, brethren, when I came to you, did not come with excellence of speech or of wisdom, declaring to you the testimony of God."],[270.43,"So this is building off of what he said, was saying at the end of chapter one."],[274.67,"He's making the point that, you know, you shouldn't be out there saying you're a follower of me"],[280.21,"I didn't show up with some great oratory trying to win followers."],[284.87,"And make disciples for myself."],[286.79,"I didn't come giving you some amazing wisdom that I figured out that other people don't have."],[292.65,"That the other apostles don't have."],[294.74,"Where I was trying to get you to follow me."],[297.64,"And since that's not what I wanted, that's not how I acted, you shouldn't be doing it."],[303.24,"For I determined not to know anything among you except Jesus Christ and him crucified."],[308.12,"This is also sort of a summary of what he had just been saying at the end of chapter one."],[312.38,"Not only that is he saying, hey, the only thing I preach to you is Christ."],[316.46,"I didn't preach Paul."],[318.24,"I didn't preach my wisdom, my system by my book."],[322.02,"Go and go and uh uh pledge to me on Patreon."],[326.82,"None of that."],[327.64,"He says, I came there, I just preached Christ."],[329.88,"And then the second part, and particularly Christ crucified, is remember, he was making the point before that not just in Christ, but from the very beginning of the Old Testament, uh, Yahweh, the God of Israel, deliberately chose to identify himself with strangers, with widows, with orphans, with the weak, with the powerless, with the poor."],[351.5,"And so it's not coincidental that when Christ was born, he was born in abject poverty, you know, to peasants of an oppressed people, and he ended his life crucified on a Roman cross."],[365.0,"So he's saying, not only did I only preach Christ, not myself, but the message I preached you about Christ was not one of, hey, here's how we're going to get wealthy and powerful, and my 12 steps to self-improvement."],[380.08,"That isn't what I was preaching."],[382.72,"So there's yeah, so there's live your best life now."],[386.53,"That's not the message I came with."],[388.13,"And so since that's not the message I came with, I don't know how you would boast about being one of my followers."],[396.05,"Boasting is the opposite of everything I preached."],[398.61,"Does he use that phrase of Christ and him crucified often, or is this the only place?"],[404.93,"Because it's very familiar to this is the famous place."],[407.73,"Ah, okay. That he preached nothing but Christ and him crucified."],[411.1,"That doesn't mean, that and and we just saw the context of that."],[415.4,"That the purpose of him crucified is the characterization he's given of the gospel."],[421.5,"Not to say, well, I didn't talk about the resurrection."],[424.86,"Or I didn't talk about the ascension."],[427.9,"Or I didn't talk about this or that."],[429.9,"All I talked about was the crucifixion."],[431.84,"That's not what he's saying, obviously."],[434.1,"But he's making the point."],[435.46,"He's who I preached, and this is how I preached him."],[441.23,"I didn't come to you trying to make him attractive."],[444.41,"I didn't proclaim him like one of the Roman gods."],[448.19,"Of power or wealth or beauty or love."],[452.03,"Here's how to get all the things you want."],[453.71,"That's not the message I preach to you"],[459.91,"He says, I was with you in weakness and fear and in much trembling."],[463.51,"And my speech and my preaching were not with persuasive words of human wisdom, but in demonstration of the spirit and of power."],[470.47,"That your faith should not be in the wisdom of men but in the power of God."],[475.59,"So he says, Look, I lived there."],[478.23,"He lived in Corinth for over a year."],[480.71,"He says, You saw when I was with you."],[483.45,"There were times when I was afraid."],[485.29,"There were times when I was sick."],[486.57,"There were times when I was we right."],[488.33,"You you didn't see me walking around with all my hair care products in order."],[493.66,"Dressed all fancy, you know, strutting down the street."],[496.46,"That that's not who I was."],[497.66,"I didn't hide. anything from you"],[499.83,"You saw the trials I was going through."],[501.85,"You saw that this is this is what the Christian life is about."],[505.61,"It's not about all those things going away."],[507.93,"It's about how you live through those things."],[510.73,"I remember this, but was he persecuted in Corinth?"],[514.25,"Yes. Yeah, that's why he ultimately had to leave."],[516.97,"Yeah. And that's probably what he's getting at with the fear, the trembling."],[522.97,"You notice he says that he talks about human wisdom."],[527.61,"Remember, Corinth is a Greek city."],[529.85,"And as we're gonna see, we already talked about a little bit last time in the introduction, but as we're gonna see over and over again as we go through this letter, a large portion of the church in Corinth are converts from paganism."],[542.45,"Not as many as probably at Colossae, which we'll see when we get to Colossians, but uh but a big percentage, a sizable percentage."],[551.01,"And this is a little unusual based on what we saw in Acts."],[554.45,"Not unusual, like unbelievable, but unusual like compared to a lot of the other churches."],[559.17,"Because remember, St."],[559.97,"Paul would first go to the synagogue in any given city until he was run out of it, basically."],[566.29,"And we saw that most of his Gentile converts were actually gotten through the synagogue."],[572.15,"They were God fearers."],[573.75,"They were Gentiles, they were Greeks or Syrians or what have you, who had some connection to the synagogue, some connection to the Hebrew scriptures."],[584.41,"Some idea of the religion of the Jewish people and some connection to it."],[585.45,"of the And one reasons they found Saint Paul's message so attractive was that they were never able to really fully become members of the Jewish community."],[603.41,"If they had wanted to, theoretically they could have."],[606.05,"They could have gone and been circumcised and gone through everything."],[608.85,"But that would have meant leaving the greater Roman community behind, leaving their families, leaving their right."],[617.89,"There were huge sacrifices, not just the physical sacrifice for men of having to get circumcised."],[622.77,"And so they were always sort of at the fringe of that community, however much it might appeal to them."],[627.97,"Whereas St. Paul, when he comes and preaches the gospel, doesn't have, there's still going to be a level to which they're going to have to withdraw from the greater Roman community."],[638.41,"But there's a lower, there are lowered barriers to entry."],[642.41,"And those lowered barriers to entry and the way that helped St."],[646.81,"Paul get converts is what made the unbelieving Jewish communities that he encountered in Acts so angry."],[655.75,"Because he's drawing off in a lot of cases, these Gentiles were the big donors to the synagogues and the ones who were endowing it."],[663.03,"He's now converting them to Christianity, and they interpreted his lowering those barriers of entry as, well, you're just chucking the law."],[672.4,"You just don't care about God's law."],[674.96,"Like you're just letting these Gentiles come in."],[675.68,"ing Without requir these things of them that the law requires."],[682.28,"This is why they got so mad at him."],[684.2,"So there's going to be there's going to be some of that reflected here in 1 Corinthians, because St."],[689.88,"Paul's going to have to make clear that those barriers are lowered a little bit in certain ways for Christianity, but they're not gone."],[699.7,"You can't just sort of add in Christ to your list of pagan gods that you honor."],[705.52,"You can't just identify as a Christian and keep living as a pagan."],[709.81,"There is a level to which they're going to have to withdraw."],[711.97,"I think we have some evidence that there were some Romans who did that, though."],[715.49,"Oh, yeah, absolutely."],[716.69,"Well, we're as we go through Fir Corstinthians, we're gonna encounter since St."],[718.53,"Paul's gonna have to say some of these things, that's clearly gonna be what's happening for some of these people"],[725.69,"He's gonna have to draw those lines."],[727.61,"But they're also, and we'll see this too, there are also some people who seem to have come straight from paganism."],[733.93,"Uh and so for them, it's gonna be even more important to have those lines delineated."],[741.37,"Of like, you can't have sort of one foot in both in both worlds."],[747.21,"Just because you didn't have to be circumcised and do all these renunciations and do all these things, that you would have had to to become a Jew doesn't mean you could just sort of move in and out."],[758.19,"Or live at the edge of the community, because that was one advantage for the Godfearers."],[761.87,"The Godfears didn't have to give anything up, they could just stay at the fringe, you know, sort of indulge it as a fascination, but that's not going to be acceptable to Saint Paul with Christianity."],[773.03,"If you're going to be part of the Christian community, you have to be a Christian, and that means not being a whole bunch of other things."],[780.31,"But as good Greeks, in Corinth, they were all about wisdom."],[787.13,"And so St."],[787.93,"Paul's saying, look, I didn't come to you like a philosopher and lay out my arguments."],[793.05,"Here are my five arguments for the existence of my God, and here's why, and here's my refutation of unbelieving Judaism, and here's my refutation of paganism, and here's my right, with his apologetic tracks and everything."],[807.15,"He says, says, That's not how I showed up to try and argue you into he, I showed up, I preached the gospel and I let the Holy Spirit do his work."],[814.95,"So if your life is changed, it's not because, you know, I came to you with better arguments than the last guy."],[822.79,"If your life is changed, that's the power of God in your life."],[826.47,"And the proof of that is I didn't do anything special."],[829.11,"I just showed up and told you the story of Jesus."],[831.65,"I just came and showed you who he was with simple words."],[835.25,"And so this transformation is a result of God."],[839.57,"That in Protestant terms, specifically Calvinism, that is referring to regeneration."],[846.85,"Is that a similar term or something that's not even approached in orthodoxy?"],[851.81,"Is that regeneration, strictly speaking, is being reborn."],[851.89,"that So in language, you know, we don't use it born again as much as some Protestant groups."],[858.33,"Okay. But I mean it comes from Christ's conversation with St."],[867.69,"Nicodemus in John's gospel."],[871.21,"Um so the concept is is there."],[874.25,"We don't get into all the Protestant debates of whether regeneration precedes faith or comes from faith and how it relates to baptism and all of these sort of technical senses."],[888.25,"It's it sort of does, it does mean something different because we're not we don't have that baggage."],[893.94,"And so in the sense of becoming a new person, yeah, and that's it."],[896.18,"Which would have been associated with obviously their baptism and receiving the Holy Spirit, because that's what St"],[901.88,"Paul associates it with."],[903.64,"But not in some kind of, he's not making some kind of mechanical statement."],[907.42,"In terms of yeah."],[909.58,"These things happen in this order."],[914.14,"Verse 6. However, we speak wisdom among those who are mature, yet not the wisdom of this age, nor of the rulers of this age who are coming to nothing."],[923.74,"So he says it's not that there's no wisdom in the gospel and in the Christian message."],[930.38,"He says that's not what he's saying."],[932.08,"He's not saying this is anti-intellectual or sub intellectual or something."],[937.44,"He's saying there is wisdom, but we speak that wisdom to the mature."],[941.08,"He's saying that's not, I didn't come and approach you with that."],[943.88,"Now you've entered the community."],[946.54,"Now you can continue to learn, and as you come to maturity, you'll learn more and come to understand more, about the ways of the ways of God."],[955.75,"You'll come to know Christ more fully."],[958.01,"This change in your life will continue to happen."],[960.91,"But that wisdom is after the fact."],[964.67,"That sounds close to something Gnostic, but I'm sure it's not, in that it sounds you could interpret it as um there's a lower level that he that Paul preaches initially, and then once you reach a certain point, you get more information to get the real stuff."],[987.91,"So I'm sure he's not saying that."],[989.99,"No, Gnosticism isn't there yet, but he is playing with, and we'll see that even more next verse."],[995.35,"He is playing with the language of mystery religion."],[997.99,"Uh-huh. He's playing with that language."],[1001.11,"And you may remember from the introduction last time why he would be playing with that language."],[1005.19,"The temple of Demeter in Corinth was the site for the mysteries of Demeter."],[1013.67,"So people came from all over place."],[1016.63,"That that's a whole Eleusis is a whole separate goddess."],[1019.99,"Oh, it's not."],[1020.79,"This is a different cult."],[1021.75,"Okay, it's not debater."],[1023.31,"Okay. Yeah, there are several mystery cults, but this is the center for the Mysteries of Demeter."],[1027.51,"So people come from all over for this"],[1031.47,"Right, sort of pagan spiritual tourism to uh to become a dish."],[1037.07,"So he's deliberately playing with that language."],[1039.49,"He's deliberately playing with that language because that's sort of why he's going where he's about to go."],[1045.01,"Uh huh. When he's saying it's not that there's no wisdom here."],[1047.97,"You shouldn't go that, like, oh, this is anti intellectual."],[1050.61,"I'm gonna go over to this pagan temple, get initiated into the mysteries, and find out the secret."],[1057.81,"Yeah, so he's saying it's not that there's wisdom there, not wisdom there."],[1062.21,"He's saying, I didn't show up and try and argue you into it."],[1065.51,"So he's moving from talking about philosophy to now talking about religion."],[1069.51,"And that's also why he mentions it.'s not the wisdom of this age, nor of the rulers of this age who are coming to nothing"],[1077.55,"Okay, the rulers of this age is not Caesar."],[1080.19,"The rulers of this age is Demeter."],[1083.15,"Uh-huh. The rulers of this age are the pagan gods who are coming to nothing."],[1089.4,"He's like, they're already finished."],[1092.78,"But this age comes to an end, so do they."],[1096.38,"And he's saying there is wisdom in Christianity, but it's not that kind of wisdom."],[1104.4,"If it's not the wisdom of this age or this world, then what is it?"],[1111.12,"It's the wisdom the age to come."],[1113.7,"If it's not this age."],[1114.66,"It's right Of another age that after this age has come to nothing, and its rulers have come to nothing."],[1125.0,"There's going to be this new."],[1126.12,"And that's where the wisdom is that St."],[1130.28,"Paul is proclaiming, is going to proclaim to them."],[1133.48,"And he's going to get into this specifically."],[1135.64,"He's sort of alluding here, he's setting up here, beginning to for chapter 15."],[1140.12,"First Corinthians 15 is where he's really going to get into the nuts and bolts ofre. deep, and we' going to slow way down"],[1151.28,"That's there. I mean, uh, 1 Corinthians 15, verse 45."],[1155.92,"There have been books and books and books written about that verse, and it's like not even a long sentence."],[1159.48,"But he's starting to plant the seeds for that"],[1162.24,"So we slow down a lot."],[1166.88,"Right? This is this is the mature stuff he's talking about."],[1170.81,"There is that."],[1171.53,"And I am going to talk about that."],[1172.73,"But it's not like when even as I say that, it's not like these things they're going to teach you over at the right."],[1180.49,"Because the rulers of this age who they're over there worshiping aren't only going to come to nothing, it's that they don't really have wisdom."],[1188.57,"They don't know the things that I'm going to tell you."],[1193.31,"The pagan gods don't know these things because they're just demons."],[1197.73,"Verse 7, but we speak the wisdom of God in a mystery, the hidden wisdom which God ordained before the ages for our glory, which none of the rulers this age knew, for had they known, they would not have crucified the Lord of glory."],[1211.37,"So Caesar wasn't there."],[1213.05,"Yeah, Pilate technically represented him."],[1216.41,"But the Jewish leaders certainly aren't the rulers of this age."],[1219.31,"So that's not that's not who he's talking about."],[1222.03,"So this is this is an important point in Saint Paul's theology."],[1228.43,"This is key to how Saint Paul understands the way Christ was prophesied in the Old Testament, and the way he appeared in the Old Testament."],[1241.71,"Because one question you could ask, well, why wasn't it more clear?"],[1246.35,"Why did God make all these vague prophecies?"],[1248.47,"Why didn't he just come out and say, hey, in this year, my son's going to be born, this is going to be his name."],[1256.33,"And just and just tell everybody, and then all of at least all of these Jewish people wouldn't be rejecting him as the Messiah, because it would have been very clear."],[1268.57,"Is it too much to say that he's separating the wheat from the chaff ahead of time?"],[1273.61,"Well, it's going a little."],[1276.33,"But that's not where St."],[1277.85,"Paul's going here, at least."],[1279.29,"Where St. Paul's going here is, and this is also related to something we see in the Gospels, especially St."],[1285.29,"Mark's Gospel, but it's in it's in all of them."],[1288.49,"Where Christ keeps telling people to keep things a secret."],[1291.37,"Oh, yes. He'll heal someone or he'll cast out demons and say, Don't tell anybody."],[1295.78,"And you're like, about him being God."],[1298.82,"Yeah, don't tell anybody."],[1300.74,"Or there are things that he's only telling the disciples who are going to become the apostles and not sharing with anybody else."],[1307.54,"Because the rulers of the time, being the demons, would not crucify them."],[1312.18,"And so for Saint Paul, this secret was being kept from even the angels and the demons, all of this all of the spiritual powers, good and bad, didn't know what was going on."],[1327.62,"And St. Paul's saying if they had known, they wouldn't have crucified him."],[1331.62,"To stop the prophecy from coming."],[1333.78,"Because that yeah, because they they would have seen it coming."],[1336.54,"They would have seen what he was doing."],[1338.54,"And so you find this all through the church fathers."],[1341.5,"St. John Chrysostom's Paschal oration, Death seized a body, discovered God."],[1347.4,"That the devil gets sort of bamboozled."],[1350.02,"Hades Hades gets tricked."],[1352.74,"Another session. And this is, and this is, you know, it in our in our hymn, The Mystery, which was hidden from everlasting and was unknown of the angels, was revealed through thee, O Theotokos to those who dwell upon the earth."],[1368.32,"That this was a secret to everybody."],[1371.6,"And so St."],[1373.04,"Paul's saying not only do these quote-unquote gods that they're off worshiping not know anything."],[1380.16,"The gospel was a surprise to them"],[1381.18,"They didn't even know this."],[1382.46,"They didn't know the gospel."],[1387.23,"That simple message I came and proclaimed to you, they didn't even know."],[1391.39,"Let alone the greater things of the faith that have become known in Christ."],[1397.15,"This is a major apologetic point over against paganism."],[1401.31,"And we're going to see St."],[1402.51,"Paul's going to come back to this idea."],[1404.51,"Again, we're still at the beginning."],[1405.71,"He's going to come back to this idea over and over again."],[1408.83,"We take for granted, we think in terms of monotheism and polytheism."],[1416.61,"Those terms did not exist until the 17th century."],[1420.61,"That's when those terms were coined."],[1422.77,"To compare different world religions."],[1423.49,"In the 17th century"],[1427.83,"They had no such idea at that time."],[1431.11,"It wasn't how many gods you believed exist."],[1434.31,"It was what god or gods did you worship."],[1437.35,"And so the the Jewish people, including St."],[1441.99,"Paul, didn't say all these gods are fictional."],[1447.56,"One of the Psalms says all the gods of the nations are demons."],[1450.92,"But he doesn't say Zeus doesn't exist, these don't exist, these are existing."],[1455.48,"Atheists today like to say, oh, well, I just believe in one less God than you do."],[1459.0,"Well, you believe it a lot less than St."],[1460.84,"Paul did. Because it wasn't that they don't exist."],[1464.98,"It's that these are spiritual powers that were that you're worshiping, are things that were created by God."],[1466.9,"They're not on his level"],[1470.78,"They're beings who God created."],[1474.22,"He's the only one worthy of worship."],[1476.14,"These are spiritual beings who are servant who are servants of his, some of whom are rebellious servants who are going to their destruction."],[1483.42,"And those are the ones you're choosing to follow when you go and worship at that idol's temple."],[1489.34,"You're not even following the good ones."],[1491.58,"You're following the ones that are headed to destruction that are coming to nothing."],[1495.66,"This clarifies a lot of uh medieval and renaissance use of the pagan gods uh as, for example, in astrology."],[1507.34,"I mean, when they're talking about the planets having influence, they mean that planet to be a god right the planets have right the names of gods but they are gods and we'll get to that in first corinthians 15 because st."],[1519.94,"Paul has basically that same understanding that there are that the angels were assigned by God to help him govern different parts of his creation the sun, the moon, the stars, the planets, all the things on earth."],[1537.47,"Nations had angels assigned to them."],[1539.63,"All these had angels as that God governs sort of through his these angels."],[1544.11,"That's part of the reason he created them."],[1546.72,"And that uh some of them fell by accepting human worship."],[1554.88,"Uh-huh. Um, and so uh the the that means by definition, all the pagan gods are among the fallen ones."],[1565.35,"And so um what you find, for example, when you read uh uh Philo, who was uh a Jewish philosopher in the first century BC, so right around the time of Christ, when he talks about the stars of the planets, he just talks about why you shouldn't worship the spiritual beings that God assigned to them."],[1587.11,"He uses the term gods."],[1588.47,"Uh huh. This is another thing that people don't realize."],[1591.75,"The term gods is used all over the place of the Old Testament."],[1594.95,"We just don't translate it that way."],[1598.23,"But St They're referred to as gods small g."],[1601.63,"People get real sketchy when you say."],[1605.07,"Paul later on here in uh chapter eight is going to use throw that term around."],[1609.87,"It didn't mean anything to them."],[1611.87,"Because the word that we translate gods just sort of means divine beings or spiritual beings."],[1616.85,"So in the old in the Old Testament, when the Witch of Endor summons up Samuel for Saul, she says, I see a god coming forward."],[1625.09,"She doesn't mean she thinks Samuel's a god."],[1627.86,"But that's the word for a spirit."],[1630.42,"Okay. This is sort of the way the Hindus think of their thousands of gods."],[1635.62,"Yeah. Yeah. Hindus are just basically classical Indo-European pagans."],[1640.66,"Uh-hhu. So there's not that much."],[1642.98,"I mean, these ideas are all through"],[1643.42,"I mean, there really isn't."],[1644.46,"I mean, you read Plato, he believed in reincarnation."],[1649.1,"These pagan ideas are shared by everybody."],[1652.92,"So, um, yeah, the difference wasn't, you know, that Jews believed there was only one God and the other ones didn't exist, and the other people believed that there were all this whole bunch of gods and goddesses who existed."],[1665.26,"The difference was how they interpreted who those different beings were."],[1670.94,"So in the Old Testament, all the time, they don't say Baal doesn't exist."],[1674.78,"In fact, they say he's Satan, basically."],[1676.94,"They say he's the devil all the time."],[1678.94,"It's deeply connected to the devil."],[1680.7,"And you find the same thing like the book of Revelation, um Saint John refers to to the high altar at Pergamos, the altar Zeus as the throne of Satan."],[1686.78,"It's not that they don't exist"],[1695.44,"He's the king of the pagan gods."],[1696.88,"Well, who's the king of the devil."],[1700.7,"So um, yeah."],[1703.5,"Yeah. So this is this is St."],[1705.1,"Paul's understanding. And say so St."],[1707.82,"Paul understands like when Christ at the end of Matthew 28 says, All power, all authority in heaven and on earth has been given to me."],[1715.43,"That means it's been taken away from all of these beings to whom God had entrusted it for to before, before he fell."],[1724.07,"And he's going to talk more about powers and principalities, referring to those beings later on in 1 Corinthians 2."],[1729.35,"But uh that Christ had taken it all back."],[1730.63,"And that's so that's why he says, no, from the bad ones"],[1735.87,"And so, well, or he's redelegated it."],[1738.43,"But that's that's um why he's saying they're coming to nothing."],[1744.45,"They're done. They don't have that authority anymore."],[1748.53,"And this is going to be where the understanding of sainthood, particularly patron sainthood, comes from in the early centuries of the church, is the idea that the saints in glory who have become sons of God, as St."],[1762.21,"Paul said in Romans 8."],[1763.65,"Sons of God is the word that's used to refer to this heavenly council of angelic beings in the Old Testament, is that they're taking the places of these. spiritual beings"],[1777.61,"And God, again, Christ is now governing the earth through the saints, which includes Saint Michael, Saint Gabriel, the angels and archangels and cherubim."],[1788.73,"And includes now glorified human beings."],[1794.65,"So it's not that you didn't pray for a good act of praying."],[1800.17,"You were praying to a demon, is what is what really was the crime."],[1806.14,"You're giving God's glory to another."],[1807.74,"Instead of giving to a God."],[1808.86,"You're giving thanks and glory to this being and not to God, who's the one who's actually providing it."],[1817.82,"Okay. Yeah Yeah."],[1819.74,"So that's this is St"],[1826.34,"Paul here has sort of dropped that quarter."],[1828.64,"That's where he's coming from."],[1829.68,"Which wouldn't have struck them as wildly as it strikes us, because we're very modern people who have have sort of logically dense and just materialist worldview."],[1838.8,"But they would have gotten exactly what he was talking about."],[1840.96,"And that's why he's playing with this mystery language and stuff."],[1844.7,"He's saying, I don't disagree with this stuff, but you're interpreting it all wrong."],[1849.26,"That's not where the wisdom is."],[1850.86,"They don't know anything."],[1852.62,"They didn't see Jesus coming."],[1854.7,"They got tricked."],[1856.99,"How do you reconcile that idea with uh like paradise and Hades?"],[1862.75,"What about it"],[1864.87,"Like the saints sort of taking the spots of God."],[1869.19,"How do you think well, paradise is just the place where God is."],[1874.15,"That's why we call the Theotokos a mystical paradise."],[1877.51,"Because God dwelt within her."],[1879.21,"So wherever God is dwelling, that's paradise."],[1881.93,"Okay. And so that's why the St."],[1884.57,"Paul calls them the dead in Christ."],[1887.75,"Says their lives are hidden in Christ."],[1890.15,"They are where Christ is."],[1891.67,"And so St."],[1892.31,"John Chrysostom, for example, flips that and says, so that means wherever Christ is, that's where the angels are, the saints, the whole host of heaven, wherever Christ is."],[1901.75,"And he's talking about the tur in terms of, you know, your little neighborhood church."],[1907.11,"When you're there in worship, it doesn't matter how dinky, how grimy, how few people you have there."],[1912.99,"Christ is there, and that means the whole hosts of heaven are there, and the angels and the saints, and you're worshiping with them."],[1918.83,"That's so that's just sort of where they go or what they do before."],[1924.19,"And this is what St."],[1924.99,"John says in Revelation."],[1926.29,"That the first resurrection, they die and they reign with Christ for a thousand years, being just a long time."],[1934.83,"That that's what they're doing."],[1936.43,"He says they reign with them, that Christ shares his rule over the earth with them."],[1941.55,"And the other thing that St."],[1942.75,"John says they're doing uh in Revelation chapter 20 is he says they're serving as priests."],[1948.83,"And it's not the word presbyter, like my title, priest."],[1951.07,"And the priests of the old covenant did two things"],[1952.15,"It's priest like old testament priest."],[1957.91,"They offered sacrifices."],[1959.19,"We know they're not offering sacrifices in paradise."],[1964.63,"They're not killing animals."],[1965.91,"And the other thing they did was intercede for the people."],[1970.39,"Okay. So what St."],[1971.84,"John is telling us is that's what the saints in glory do."],[1975.28,"Click. They rule on behalf of Christ and they intercede for those still on earth."],[1984.4,"That clarifies paradise, but we say that God is everywhere."],[1988.82,"Um, what about, you know, like on the college campus or something, um, or in our homes."],[1995.38,"Um the saints and angels there also"],[2000.38,"And further question does this mean that Hades is the place where God is not?"],[2006.3,"Okay. Answer first question."],[2008.54,"Yes, when we're in worship."],[2010.7,"If I'm mowing the ground."],[2012.94,"Well, well, what do you mean by there?"],[2015.98,"Well I mean they're not absent."],[2018.3,"Yeah. But see, there's God's presence and there's his presence."],[2022.59,"What I mean by that is let's let's look at the old deser example."],[2026.43,"Uh huh. God was present in the temple in a way that he wasn't present in the other buildings in Jerusalem."],[2032.33,"Uh-hhu. Okay. Okay."],[2033.33,"Gotcha. Or in other cities."],[2034.79,"That doesn't mean he was absent, in those other places."],[2038.08,"But the veil between the other things."],[2039.4,"But there's a different, there's a different kind of presence."],[2045.54,"Yeah. So answer the second question."],[2048.98,"No. God is everywhere."],[2050.66,"And that's, I mean, all through the Psalms, even if I go down to Sheol, you are there."],[2056.88,"The problem for people who hate God is not that God isn't there."],[2061.92,"The problem with people that hate God is God is there and they hate him."],[2067.82,"And so his holiness and his glory are destructive and painful to someone who hates him."],[2078.02,"Um and that's that's what God's wrath is."],[2081.56,"It's his holiness and his uh and his glory when you don't want that and when or when you're corrupted by sin and not ready to receive that."],[2096.6,"And so the the the the whole language of repentance is that that same fire of God's holiness and his glory burns us too, and it's not a pleasant experience, but it burns away the the sin and the dross and the right and purifies us as opposed to consuming us."],[2119.56,"So that's the distinction."],[2122.12,"Okay, that's about half a ton of theology."],[2125.48,"Yeah. Yes. At least I know how to get people to not ask any more questions."],[2134.0,"But yeah, so here the important thing that St."],[2136.72,"Paul is laying down for them is look, you going there is going to the wrong place."],[2142.8,"They don't know anything."],[2145.49,"They don't know anything as proven by what happened with Christ."],[2149.41,"And he's going to develop these ideas as he goes through because this whole idea of people trying to straddle paganism and Christianity is a major issue in Corinth."],[2158.61,"For us, this is even a bigger readjustment."],[2162.71,"Because we've not only kind of assumed, but we've probably been actually taught that St."],[2168.71,"Paul as a Jew shouldn't believe. what he obviously believes in his teaching here"],[2174.83,"Or is just saying here casually, as if it's uncontroversial."],[2179.79,"So verse 9, but as it is written, I has not seen nor ear heard, nor have entered into the heart of man the things which God has prepared for those who love him."],[2189.07,"So he refers back to Isaiah, Isaiah 64."],[2193.41,"That this was this secret."],[2195.09,"Saying Isaiah, remember when he prophesied, he said God had this secret that he had prepared for those who loved him."],[2204.45,"We now know what that secret was."],[2209.25,"But God has revealed them to it."],[2211.09,"Now notice that them is added."],[2212.45,"So it could be it, it could be him."],[2214.37,"God has revealed it to us through his spirit"],[2218.94,"For the spirit searches all things."],[2221.42,"Yes, the deep things of God."],[2223.74,"For what man knows the things of a man except the spirit of the man which is in him?"],[2227.82,"Even so, no one knows the things of God except the Spirit of God."],[2231.68,"So he's saying, Well, how do how do we know these things?"],[2235.29,"This is very rees."],[2238.89,"He says, How do we know these things?"],[2240.91,"Is it that I'm so smart and I'm so wise and I'm so clever?"],[2243.65,"No, we just went over that."],[2245.19,"I'm not. I said it was the power of the Holy Spirit."],[2248.33,"He says, so that that's how I've come to know these things."],[2252.65,"That's how you can come to know these things."],[2254.57,"The Holy Spirit now dwells in you."],[2256.74,"And why does how does the Holy Spirit know them?"],[2259.14,"Well, who knows you better than you?"],[2264.32,"Who knows you better than your spirit?"],[2266.56,"My wife knows me pretty well, but I know me better."],[2272.97,"And so the Spirit of God knows all the things of God."],[2278.97,"So if you have the Spirit within you, you already have access to all of God."],[2287.05,"Meaning what? Meaning you don't have to be initiated into some mystery to find something else out."],[2293.21,"They don't know what you want to know in the first place."],[2296.73,"But not only do they not know it, you already have access to it."],[2300.05,"So right. You've already got it."],[2301.97,"When you hear the truth being spoken, you hear it, you understand it."],[2307.09,"Someone without the spirit, it's vanity."],[2310.05,"It's right. Or they'll twist it, or but also then the means for you to learn more and to understand these things is what?"],[2320.45,"It's going to be living by the spirit."],[2322.93,"It's going to be living by the spirit and following the spirit."],[2325.97,"Not seeking after some esoteric mystical experience."],[2330.39,"In these mystery rites."],[2332.07,"It's the unfound in books."],[2335.69,"Or rituals. Or, you know, pagan rituals or magic."],[2339.87,"In Corinth. This isn't. the way to get those those secrets"],[2346.95,"Now we have received not the spirit of the world, but the spirit who is from God, that we might know the things that have been freely given to us by God."],[2356.31,"He talks about the spirit of the world, given the context we're in."],[2359.97,"He's talking about demonic possession."],[2362.77,"To us, demonic possession is very clearly a bad thing."],[2367.01,"I wager to say no one in this room would like to be possessed by a demon."],[2371.41,"In Corinth in the first century, very many people would very much have liked to have been possessed by a demon."],[2377.97,"Because we take for granted that the word demon is a pejorative."],[2381.59,"For us, demon means evil spirit."],[2383.43,"For them, demon didn't mean evil spirit."],[2385.67,"For them, it just meant a spirit, a god, a divine spirit."],[2386.63,"Pagan gods take frequently"],[2390.19,"Oh, yes. Take you away."],[2394.85,"This was a common phenomenon."],[2397.41,"Socrates. Yeah. Plato's in Plato's Apology and in the Republic, uh, Socrates talks about his demonic sign, the demon who's lived in him since he was young, and who whispers wisdom to him and advises him on how to proceed."],[2415.01,"And he brings this up in the Apology to defend himself, to tell the Athenians who are about to execute him, look, I'm guided by a power greater than all of you, as a defense."],[2428.95,"So the that oracle at Delphi was possessed by Apollo."],[2435.63,"This was a good thing."],[2437.55,"And not only in uh in those cases, but for example, uh the very, very popular cult of Dionysus at this time in history, or Bacchus, if you're in Rome."],[2452.21,"And the Bacchanalia, which they would have, was essentially a massive public festival of sexual orgies and drinking."],[2462.79,"The purpose and climax of which were was people being possessed by the back eye, by these spirits."],[2471.43,"Don't you then tear an animal apart with your teeth?"],[2473.83,"Yes, they would do things like that."],[2474.47,"This was a spiritual experience"],[2476.19,"And this was this was good."],[2479.47,"These are people who are spiritual but not religious."],[2485.55,"So like Mardi Grande Worlds."],[2487.29,"So I never ate a raw hammer."],[2492.09,"All the years I lived in New Orleans."],[2494.49,"But yeah, so this was this is what they were after."],[2497.05,"This is why we already encountered this a little bit in the book of Acts."],[2499.53,"Remember when there was that slave girl who was demon-possessed and would like tell fortunes?"],[2504.26,"It was perfect."],[2505.06,"And St. Paul comes and casts the demon out of her, and her owners get all angry because he just ruined their way of making a living."],[2515.94,"So it was that same kind of that same. kind of dynamic"],[2519.9,"When Christ casts demons out, usually the demon is is obviously harming the person."],[2526.78,"Like the man is possessed by Legion."],[2529.02,"Well, that's in the context of I'll get well, I'll get to Legion in a second, but that's primarily in the context of Judea and Galilee."],[2536.78,"So you're in a Jewish context."],[2539.42,"And the Jewish understanding of who these spirits were as unclean spirits was very different than the Greek and Roman understanding."],[2548.48,"Now, you may have noticed, like in the gospel reading this past Sunday, when we when we read it about the Gaterenes, that when Jesus casts the demons out of him, they don't all show up and say, Oh, this is wonderful."],[2560.4,"They tell him to leave."],[2561.84,"Yeah. Because they're terrified and they don't understand what's going on"],[2569.4,"So that's a Gentile context at the same time."],[2573.56,"And so there is, there is, and this is important as we're going through 1 Corinthians here, there's a difference in the way uh Saint Paul uses the word demon and the way the Synoptic Gospels use the word demon."],[2586.84,"St. John's Gospel doesn't use it."],[2588.44,"There's no exorcisms in St."],[2589.88,"John's Gospel for whatever reason."],[2592.2,"But uh in the Synoptic Gospels, they had a different understanding."],[2596.36,"I don't want to go too far down this rabbit hole because it's kind of a wacky rabbit hole."],[2601.72,"I say wacky in the sense that this is one of those things."],[2604.44,"I mean, I already talked about giants last week on the internet."],[2607.16,"So uh but it's actually related."],[2610.08,"In the book of Jubilees, I'll just do this quickly."],[2613.68,"In the Book of Jubilees, which was a very popular book at this time, Josephus in his history of the Jewish people, there's more of it from the Book of Jubilees than there is from the text of the Old Testament."],[2626.56,"And he was a Pharisee."],[2629.04,"There are more copies of Jubilees in the Dead Sea Scrolls at Qumran than of any book in the Old Testament except for Genesis."],[2642.24,"That's how popular it was at this time."],[2644.32,"And in the book of Jubilees, what happens is when God sends the flood and then a bunch of people culminating in Joshua and then King David to kill all the giants, to kill all the Nephilim."],[2656.68,"They're all being God is throwing them all into the abyss with their parents."],[2662.41,"Confining them. And that gets made reference to it."],[2666.33,"Both uh St."],[2667.53,"Peter and 2 Peter, Jude makes reference to it, to them being imprisoned, and uh St."],[2672.09,"Peter uses the word Tartarus from Greek mythology."],[2675.45,"Um but that talks about them being imprisoned."],[2678.49,"And one of them, who in the book of Jubilees is named Mastema, uh sort of tries cuts a deal with God and says, Hey, you know, why don't you let some of us stick around on earth as spirits, as disembodied spirits, and allow us to sort of torment the wicked?"],[2698.85,"And so God takes the deal and says, Okay, I'll let like 10% of you hang around earth for a while, you know, and to torment the wicked, and it says that God was doing this because he to use them to bring about repentance."],[2714.77,"Okay, the idea was he was like so that he could use them to bring people to repentance through them tormenting people."],[2721.25,"But then when the end of the age came, right into the abyss with you."],[2725.78,"So that's it."],[2727.62,"And so that's where your average Jewish person in the first century thought demons came from."],[2733.38,"And you see this reflected in the Gospels."],[2736.1,"Like, again, we'll go back to St."],[2738.18,"Luke's Gospel of the Gathering."],[2739.7,"What is the demon?"],[2740.38,"What did the demons say?"],[2742.22,"Don't cast us into the abyss."],[2744.46,"Have you come to torment us before the time?"],[2746.86,"Before the time."],[2748.04,"Wow. So, yeah, so that idea kind of gets referenced."],[2752.44,"So the synoptic gospels are working with that understanding of demons."],[2757.48,"St. Paul is using it in the Greco-Roman way to refer to these spirits, especially territorial spirits."],[2765.08,"And a major place where it gets used that way in the Old Testament, in the Greek."],[2771.16,"I'm getting deep now."],[2772.52,"Anyway, in the Greek of Deuteronomy 32, when it says, it's near the end of chapter 32, when it says, it's usually translated in English that the Israelites turned from worshiping Yahweh and sacrificed to beings that are not God."],[2790.88,"Sometimes it's translated demons in English."],[2793.04,"And that's following the Greek."],[2794.32,"The Greek uses the word demons there."],[2796.24,"The word that's in the Hebrew is not really a Hebrew word."],[2799.04,"The word that's in the Hebrew is Shedim, which is a Hebrew pluralization of the Babylonian word word shedu, which refers to a territorial spirit."],[2808.88,"A spirit or a god that governs a particular piece of territory."],[2812.56,"So St. Paul, and that's the sense that the Greeks understood it in."],[2815.76,"If you read Plato's Critias and his laws, he says that all the gods got assigned by uh a greater God."],[2822.56,"Sure, every city has a god."],[2824.08,"Yeah. Back in the distant past, in a in a golden age, Plato says there was this greater God who assigned all of the nations. and all the places and all the cities to these lesser gods to govern them"],[2836.12,"And he even says at first they were beneficent and wonderful, and then they all kind of turned crazy."],[2841.16,"It's really interesting if Plato."],[2842.84,"But yeah, that's the Critias and his his uh dialogue on the laws."],[2847.16,"But so that that was part of the Greco-Roman view."],[2849.64,"And that's when St."],[2850.36,"Paul uses the term, he's referring to that whole set of traditions and understandings."],[2855.24,"As we've seen here when he's talking about the rulers of this age, in this kind of thing."],[2859.73,"But so all that is now that I've gone down that rabbit trail, all that is to say, when he's talking about the spirit we have living within, us is not the spirit of this age, he's talking to those kind of rituals that involved possession."],[2871.09,"He's saying, You're not gonna get this wisdom from that either."],[2874.93,"That's not the spirit we have."],[2876.29,"We have. the Holy Spirit, God's own spirit, dwelling within us"],[2879.93,"So his whole point here is that in that pagan world out there, and he's going to be applying that as we go, but in that pagan world, there's nothing out there in those pagan mysteries and the wisdom they're trying to promise you."],[2890.89,"There's nothing there, they don't know anything."],[2893.21,"They're coming to nothing."],[2894.97,"And you already know more than they know."],[2897.93,"In fact, you have access through the Holy Spirit and through living by the Spirit to all the things of God, the true God who created everything, including those things that those people are worshiping instead of him."],[2910.57,"So that's sort of the, and again, he's laying the groundwork for things he's going to unpack later."],[2916.89,"But this is the beginning of that."],[2918.97,"Listen next time as Father Stephen DeYo.ung continues his study of the scriptures on the Whole Counsel of God"],[2926.21,"Father Stephen's email address is wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."],[2931.57,"That's wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."]],"o":[{"t":20.88,"lv":2,"h":"Recap: Corinth and the factions","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Picking up at <b>1 Corinthians 2:1</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Last time: <b>Corinth's history</b> (intro), then <b>chapter 1</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Paul <b>plants seeds</b> of the whole epistle in the opening - intro, then unpacks themes</li><li class=\"d0\">Church in Corinth has <b>a lot of problems</b></li><li class=\"d1\">one: <b>factions</b> - unintended \"cults of personality\"</li><li class=\"d1\">parties of <b>Paul</b>, <b>Peter</b>, <b>Apollos</b></li><li class=\"d1\">some one-upping: \"you follow only <b>Christ</b>\" - still pitting people against each other</li><li class=\"d0\">Paul denounces it: never intended it</li><li class=\"d1\">Paul <b>didn't die</b> for them, didn't <b>forgive their sins</b>, not \"the gospel of Paul\"</li><li class=\"d1\">all <b>one in Christ</b> - only Christ can do these things</li><li class=\"d0\">Someone from the community told him the news - \"who the <b>rat</b> was\" (the intro)</li><li class=\"d0\">His approach: not just chiding, but <b>remind them who they are in Christ</b> and who God called them to be</li><li class=\"d1\">\"this is the destiny ahead of you\" - live up to it; implication: <b>right now we're not</b></li></ul>"},{"t":262.49,"lv":2,"h":"1 Corinthians 2:1-2 - Christ and him crucified","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>2:1</b>: came <b>not with excellence of speech or wisdom</b>, declaring the testimony of God</li><li class=\"d1\">builds off end of ch. 1: no great oratory to <b>win followers</b>, no amazing wisdom the other apostles lack</li><li class=\"d1\">since that's not how he acted, <b>they shouldn't</b> be doing it</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>2:2</b>: determined to know <b>nothing but Jesus Christ and him crucified</b></li><li class=\"d1\">preached Christ, not <b>Paul</b>, not \"my system, my book\" - \"pledge to me on <b>Patreon</b>\": none of that</li><li class=\"d1\">why <b>crucified</b>: Yahweh chose to identify with <b>strangers, widows, orphans, the weak, the poor</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Christ born in <b>abject poverty</b>, to peasants of an oppressed people; died on a <b>Roman cross</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not \"how to get wealthy and powerful\", \"12 steps\", \"<b>live your best life now</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">so how could you <b>boast</b> about being my follower? Boasting = opposite of what I preached</li><li class=\"d0\">Q: is that phrase used often? - <b>this is the famous place</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not saying he never preached resurrection or ascension - the <b>characterization of the gospel</b></li><li class=\"d1\">didn't make him attractive, didn't proclaim him like a <b>Roman god</b> of power, wealth, beauty, love</li></ul>"},{"t":459.91,"lv":2,"h":"2:3-5 - Weakness, fear, and the power of the Spirit","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>2:3-5</b>: in <b>weakness, fear, much trembling</b>; preaching in <b>demonstration of the Spirit and of power</b> - faith in <b>God's power</b>, not men's wisdom</li><li class=\"d0\">He lived in Corinth <b>over a year</b></li><li class=\"d1\">they saw him afraid, <b>sick</b>, weary</li><li class=\"d1\">not strutting around with \"hair care products\", dressed fancy</li><li class=\"d1\">hid nothing: saw the <b>trials</b> he went through</li><li class=\"d1\">Christian life = not those things going away, but <b>how you live through them</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Q: persecuted in Corinth? - yes, <b>why he had to leave</b>; probably the fear and trembling</li><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>Human wisdom</b>\": Corinth a <b>Greek city</b></li></ul>"},{"t":522.97,"lv":3,"h":"Pagan converts vs. God-fearers","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Large part of the church = <b>converts from paganism</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not as many as <b>Colossae</b>, but a sizable percentage</li><li class=\"d1\">unusual compared to other churches</li><li class=\"d0\">In Acts Paul went to the <b>synagogue</b> first - Gentile converts mostly came via <b>God-fearers</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Greeks, Syrians etc. with some connection to <b>Hebrew scriptures</b></li><li class=\"d1\">could never fully join: <b>circumcision</b>, leaving Roman community, family</li><li class=\"d1\">stuck at the <b>fringe</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Gospel = <b>lowered barriers to entry</b> - made Jewish communities angry</li><li class=\"d1\">he was drawing off the <b>big donors</b> who endowed synagogues</li><li class=\"d1\">accused: \"just chucking the law\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Reflected in 1 Cor: barriers lowered, <b>not gone</b></li><li class=\"d1\">can't add Christ to your list of <b>pagan gods</b></li><li class=\"d1\">can't identify as Christian and <b>keep living as a pagan</b></li></ul>"},{"t":711.97,"lv":3,"h":"Straddling two worlds","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: evidence some Romans did that? - <b>absolutely</b>; Paul will <b>draw the lines</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Some came <b>straight from paganism</b> - lines even more important</li><li class=\"d0\">\"Can't have <b>one foot in both worlds</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">God-fearers could stay at the fringe, <b>indulge it as a fascination</b> - not acceptable with Christianity</li><li class=\"d1\">to be Christian = <b>not being a whole bunch of other things</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Greeks were <b>all about wisdom</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Paul didn't come as a <b>philosopher</b>: five arguments for my God, refutation of Judaism, refutation of paganism - <b>apologetic tracts</b></li><li class=\"d1\">preached the gospel, let the <b>Holy Spirit</b> do his work</li><li class=\"d1\">changed life = <b>power of God</b>, not better arguments than the last guy</li><li class=\"d1\">proof: \"I didn't do anything special\" - just <b>told the story of Jesus</b> in simple words</li></ul>"},{"t":839.57,"lv":3,"h":"Q&amp;A: regeneration","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: Calvinist term - <b>regeneration</b> - Orthodox equivalent?</li><li class=\"d1\">regeneration = <b>being reborn</b>; we say \"born again\" less than some Protestants</li><li class=\"d1\">comes from Christ and <b>Nicodemus</b> (John)</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>concept is there</b>, without the Protestant debates</li><li class=\"d1\">debates: regeneration before or from faith; relation to <b>baptism</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"we don't have that <b>baggage</b>\" - so it means something different</li><li class=\"d0\">Sense of <b>becoming a new person</b></li><li class=\"d1\">associated with <b>baptism</b> and receiving the Holy Spirit - what Paul ties it to</li><li class=\"d1\">but not a <b>mechanical statement</b> - \"these things happen in this order\"</li></ul>"},{"t":914.14,"lv":2,"h":"2:6 - Wisdom for the mature; mystery language","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>2:6</b>: we speak wisdom <b>among the mature</b>, not the wisdom of <b>this age</b> nor of the <b>rulers of this age</b> coming to nothing</li><li class=\"d1\">not <b>anti-intellectual</b>: there is wisdom in the gospel</li><li class=\"d1\">not what he came to them with: <b>after you enter</b> the community you keep learning, come to know Christ more fully</li><li class=\"d1\">\"that wisdom is <b>after the fact</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Q: sounds <b>Gnostic</b> - lower level first, then the real stuff?</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Gnosticism isn't there yet</b>, but he's playing with <b>mystery religion</b> language</li><li class=\"d1\">why: <b>temple of Demeter</b> in Corinth - center of her mysteries</li><li class=\"d1\">people came from everywhere - \"pagan <b>spiritual tourism</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">(not Eleusis - several mystery cults)</li><li class=\"d0\">He's saying: don't go off to be <b>initiated</b> and find the secret</li><li class=\"d0\">Moving from <b>philosophy</b> to <b>religion</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1077.55,"lv":3,"h":"Rulers of this age = pagan gods","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">\"Rulers of this age\" is <b>not Caesar</b> - it's <b>Demeter</b></li><li class=\"d1\">the <b>pagan gods</b> coming to nothing - \"already finished\"</li><li class=\"d1\">this age ends, so do they</li><li class=\"d0\">Real wisdom = <b>wisdom of the age to come</b></li><li class=\"d1\">its rulers come to nothing too; a <b>new</b> age</li><li class=\"d0\">Setting up <b>1 Corinthians 15</b> - slow way down there</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>15:45</b>: books written on one short verse</li><li class=\"d0\">\"The mature stuff\" - not what they'll teach you over at the temple</li><li class=\"d1\">pagan gods don't have wisdom: <b>\"just demons\"</b> - don't know what I'll tell you</li></ul>"},{"t":1197.73,"lv":2,"h":"2:7-8 - The hidden wisdom no ruler knew","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>2:7-8</b>: wisdom of God in a <b>mystery</b>, <b>hidden before the ages</b> for our glory; none of the rulers knew - else would <b>not have crucified the Lord of glory</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Not Caesar (Pilate only represented him); <b>not Jewish leaders</b> either</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Key to Paul's theology</b> of how Christ was prophesied in the OT</li><li class=\"d0\">Q: why so vague? why not say year and name? - \"separating wheat from chaff ahead of time?\" - going a little far</li><li class=\"d0\">Paul's point: connects to Gospels, esp. <b>Mark</b> - Christ tells people to <b>keep it secret</b></li><li class=\"d1\">heal / cast out demon: \"<b>don't tell anybody</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">some things only for the disciples-to-be-apostles</li><li class=\"d0\">Secret kept even from <b>angels and demons</b> - <b>spiritual powers good and bad</b></li><li class=\"d1\">had they known, they'd have seen it coming</li><li class=\"d0\">Church fathers: <b>Chrysostom's Paschal homily</b> - \"Death seized a body, discovered <b>God</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">devil <b>bamboozled</b>, Hades <b>tricked</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Hymn: \"The <b>mystery</b> hidden from everlasting, unknown to angels, revealed through thee, O <b>Theotokos</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Major apologetic point</b> against paganism - they didn't even know the <b>gospel</b></li><li class=\"d1\">he'll come back to it again and again</li></ul>"},{"t":1402.51,"lv":2,"h":"No monotheism/polytheism; the gods as created beings","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">We think <b>monotheism vs. polytheism</b> - terms coined in the <b>17th century</b></li><li class=\"d1\">ancients: not how many gods exist, but <b>which god(s) you worship</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Paul didn't say the gods are fictional</li><li class=\"d1\">Psalm: \"all the gods of the nations are <b>demons</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">atheist \"I believe in <b>one less God</b>\" - you believe a lot less than Paul</li><li class=\"d0\">Spiritual powers <b>created by God</b>, not on his level</li><li class=\"d1\">servants - some <b>rebellious</b>, headed to destruction</li><li class=\"d1\">worship there = following the ones <b>coming to nothing</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Fits medieval/Renaissance <b>astrology</b> - planets as gods</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>1 Cor 15</b>: angels assigned to <b>sun, moon, stars, planets</b>, earth; <b>nations had angels</b></li><li class=\"d1\">some <b>fell by accepting human worship</b> → all pagan gods are among the fallen</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Philo</b> (Jewish philosopher, 1st c. BC): don't worship the beings assigned to stars; uses the word <b>gods</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1587.11,"lv":3,"h":"\"Gods\" in the Old Testament; Hindus, Baal, Pergamum","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Word <b>gods</b> all over the OT - we just don't translate it that way</li><li class=\"d1\">small-g; <b>chapter 8</b> Paul throws the term around</li><li class=\"d1\">means <b>divine / spiritual beings</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Witch of Endor</b>: sees \"a god coming forward\" = <b>Samuel</b> - word for a spirit</li><li class=\"d0\">Hindus ~ <b>classical Indo-European pagans</b>; Plato believed in <b>reincarnation</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Difference: not one God vs. many - <b>how they interpreted who those beings were</b></li><li class=\"d1\">OT: not \"Baal doesn't exist\" - he's <b>Satan</b>, basically</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Revelation</b>: altar of Zeus at <b>Pergamos</b> = \"throne of <b>Satan</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Matthew 28</b>: \"all authority in heaven and on earth given to me\"</li><li class=\"d1\">taken from the beings God entrusted it to <b>before they fell</b>; or <b>redelegated</b></li><li class=\"d1\">more on <b>powers and principalities</b> later in 1 Cor 2</li></ul>"},{"t":1744.45,"lv":2,"h":"Origin of patron sainthood","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Rulers \"coming to nothing\" - <b>no authority anymore</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Source of <b>patron sainthood</b> in early church</li><li class=\"d1\">saints in glory = <b>sons of God</b> (<b>Romans 8</b>) = word for the <b>heavenly council</b> in the OT</li><li class=\"d1\">taking the places of those spiritual beings</li><li class=\"d1\">Christ governs the earth through <b>saints</b>: Michael, Gabriel, angels, archangels, cherubim, now <b>glorified humans</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Pagan <b>crime</b>: giving God's glory and thanks to a demon instead of <b>God</b>, who actually provides</li><li class=\"d0\">Strikes us oddly - <b>materialist</b> worldview - but <b>they'd have got it</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"I don't disagree with this stuff, but you're <b>interpreting it wrong</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">they got <b>tricked</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1856.99,"lv":2,"h":"Q&amp;A: paradise, Hades, God's presence","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: how reconcile with <b>paradise and Hades</b>?</li><li class=\"d1\">paradise = <b>where God is</b> - Theotokos \"<b>mystical paradise</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Paul: the dead in Christ - lives <b>hidden in Christ</b>; they are where Christ is</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Chrysostom</b>: wherever Christ is, angels, saints, whole host of heaven</li><li class=\"d1\">your <b>dinky church</b>: Christ is there → whole hosts of heaven worship with you</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Revelation 20</b>: first resurrection - they <b>reign with Christ</b> and serve as <b>priests</b></li><li class=\"d1\">OT priests: <b>sacrifice</b> and <b>intercede</b>; no animals in paradise</li><li class=\"d1\">saints in glory <b>rule on behalf of Christ</b> and <b>intercede</b> for those on earth</li><li class=\"d0\">Q: God is everywhere - on a college campus, in our homes?</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>God's presence vs. his presence</b>: in the <b>temple</b> differently than other Jerusalem buildings; a different kind of presence</li></ul>"},{"t":2045.54,"lv":3,"h":"Is Hades where God is not?","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Q: is Hades where God is not? - <b>No</b>, God is everywhere</li><li class=\"d1\">Psalms: \"even if I go down to <b>Sheol</b>, you are there\"</li><li class=\"d1\">problem for those who hate God: <b>God is there and they hate him</b></li><li class=\"d1\">his <b>holiness and glory</b> destructive and painful to one who hates him = <b>God's wrath</b></li><li class=\"d1\">when <b>corrupted by sin</b>, not ready to receive it</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Repentance</b> language: same fire burns us, not pleasant</li><li class=\"d1\">burns away <b>sin and dross</b>, purifies rather than <b>consuming</b></li><li class=\"d0\">\"About <b>half a ton of theology</b>\" - \"how to get people to not ask any more questions\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Takeaway for Corinth: <b>going to the wrong place</b> - they know nothing, <b>proved by Christ</b></li><li class=\"d1\">straddling paganism and Christianity = <b>major issue in Corinth</b></li><li class=\"d0\">For us a bigger readjustment: we're taught Paul as a <b>Jew</b> shouldn't believe this - he says it <b>casually, uncontroversial</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2174.83,"lv":2,"h":"2:9-12 - Revealed by the Spirit","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>2:9</b>: \"eye has not seen...\" - from <b>Isaiah 64</b></li><li class=\"d1\">God's <b>secret prepared for those who love him</b> - now we know it</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>2:10</b>: \"God has revealed <b>them</b>\" (them added - could be <b>it</b>) to us <b>through his Spirit</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>2:10-11</b>: Spirit searches <b>deep things of God</b>; who knows a man but the <b>spirit of the man</b>?</li><li class=\"d1\">how do we know? not because I'm <b>smart and clever</b> - <b>power of the Holy Spirit</b></li><li class=\"d1\">same Spirit <b>dwells in you</b></li><li class=\"d1\">who knows you better than <b>you</b>? \"My wife knows me pretty well, but I know me better\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Spirit knows the things of God → you have <b>access to all of God</b></li><li class=\"d0\">No need to be <b>initiated into some mystery</b> - they don't know it anyway</li><li class=\"d0\">When truth is spoken you <b>hear and understand</b>; without the Spirit it's <b>vanity</b>, or they twist it</li><li class=\"d0\">To learn more: <b>live by the Spirit</b> - not <b>esoteric experience</b>, books, rituals, magic, <b>mystery rites</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2346.95,"lv":2,"h":"2:12 - The spirit of the world: possession","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>2:12</b>: received not the <b>spirit of the world</b>, but the Spirit <b>from God</b>, that we may know what is freely given</li><li class=\"d0\">Spirit of the world = <b>demonic possession</b></li><li class=\"d1\">to us clearly bad - nobody here wants to be possessed</li><li class=\"d1\">in 1st-c. Corinth <b>many would have liked it</b>: *daimon* not pejorative, just <b>divine spirit</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Socrates</b>: <b>demonic sign</b> since youth whispers wisdom (Apology, Republic) - used as defense before Athenians</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Oracle at Delphi</b> possessed by <b>Apollo</b> - good thing</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Dionysus / Bacchus</b> cult: Bacchanalia = public festival of <b>orgies and drinking</b></li><li class=\"d1\">climax = being <b>possessed</b>; tearing an animal apart - \"a spiritual experience\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"<b>spiritual but not religious</b>\"; Mardi Gras (New Orleans)</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Acts</b>: slave girl with fortune-telling spirit - Paul casts it out, owners angry</li></ul>"},{"t":2519.9,"lv":2,"h":"Demons: Gentile vs. Jewish understanding","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Gospels: demon usually <b>harming the person</b> - <b>Legion</b></li><li class=\"d1\">that's a <b>Jewish context</b> (Judea, Galilee) - different understanding from Greek/Roman</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Gerasenes</b> (last Sunday's Gospel): Gentile context - they <b>tell Jesus to leave</b>, terrified</li><li class=\"d0\">Paul's use of *demon* differs from the <b>Synoptics</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>John</b> has no exorcisms</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Jubilees</b> - very popular: Josephus uses it more than OT text; <b>most copies at Qumran</b> after Genesis</li><li class=\"d1\">flood and <b>David</b> kill the <b>Nephilim/giants</b> → thrown into <b>abyss</b> with their parents (2 Peter, Jude; <b>Tartarus</b>)</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Mastema</b> deals: leave 10% as disembodied spirits to <b>torment the wicked</b></li><li class=\"d1\">God uses them to bring <b>repentance</b>; at end of age, into the abyss</li><li class=\"d1\">origin of demons for <b>first-century Jews</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Luke's Gerasene: \"don't cast us into the <b>abyss</b>... torment us <b>before the time</b>\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2752.44,"lv":3,"h":"Paul's Greco-Roman usage: territorial spirits","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Synoptics work with the Jubilees understanding; <b>Paul</b> uses Greco-Roman sense - <b>territorial spirits</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Deuteronomy 32</b> (Greek): sacrificed to <b>demons</b> (not God)</li><li class=\"d1\">Hebrew <b>Shedim</b> = pluralization of Babylonian <b>shedu</b> = <b>territorial spirit</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Plato</b> (Critias, Laws): greater God <b>assigned nations, places, cities</b> to lesser gods</li><li class=\"d1\">at first beneficent, then \"all turned crazy\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Paul invokes this whole tradition - <b>rulers of this age</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Not the spirit of this age</b> = pagan <b>possession rituals</b> - not the wisdom source</li><li class=\"d0\">We have the <b>Holy Spirit</b>, God's own</li><li class=\"d0\">Pagan mysteries: <b>nothing there</b>, coming to nothing</li><li class=\"d1\">you know <b>more than they</b>; through the Spirit you have access to <b>all things of the true God</b></li><li class=\"d1\">groundwork for what he <b>unpacks later</b></li></ul>"}]});
